  "$comment": "How every semantic colour role derives from a brand (specs/brand-theming.md). A brand is a light colour, a dark colour and an optional accent, all 8 bit sRGB. Colour maths: convert sRGB to OKLab (Ottosson 2020 matrices, standard sRGB transfer function), interpolate linearly, convert back, clamp each channel to the range 0 to 1 and round channel × 255 half up to an integer. Every mix starts from the 8 bit input colours.",
  "version": 1,
  "spec": "https://github.com/BindsHQ/stance/blob/main/specs/brand-theming.md",
  "binds": {
    "name": "Binds",
    "light": "#FCF6EB",
    "dark": "#140C2E"
  },
  "kinds": {
    "light": "The brand's light colour.",
    "dark": "The brand's dark colour.",
    "ink": "Step `step` of the ink scale: light mixed toward dark by the position of that step in `ink`.",
    "literal": "A fixed colour that does not depend on the brand (status colours).",
    "derive": "`from` (light or dark) mixed toward `toward` (white, black, light, dark, or null for no mix) by `amount`, with alpha `alpha`.",
    "accentFit": "Without an accent: `fallback`. With one: start from the accent the theme names in `accent` (a single accent colour serves every theme). use text or ring: fit against the resolved roles in `against`, moving L toward `toward` (black gives L 0, white gives L 1). use fill: pick the foreground first (light or dark, whichever has the higher contrast on the starting accent, light wins a tie), fit against that one colour, toward black (L 0) when the relative luminance of the foreground is higher than that of the start, otherwise toward white (L 1). Fitting: see `fit`.",
    "accentShade": "Without an accent: `fallback`. With one: the resolved role `of` mixed in OKLab by `amount` toward the brand colour (light or dark) that is not the resolved role `awayFrom` (toward dark when `awayFrom` equals light, otherwise toward light).",
    "accentForeground": "Light or dark, whichever has the higher WCAG 2 contrast ratio on the resolved role `on`. Light wins a tie."
  },
  "fit": {
    "iterations": 32,
    "steps": [
      "Keep the starting colour OKLab a and b; only L changes. Every candidate is converted to 8 bit hex (clamp, round half up) before its contrast is measured.",
      "A candidate passes when its WCAG 2 contrast ratio against every target colour is at least `min`.",
      "If the starting colour passes, use it unchanged.",
      "Otherwise, if the colour at the target L (0 or 1) fails too, use that colour.",
      "Otherwise bisect exactly 32 times with lo = start L (failing) and hi = target L (passing): mid = (lo + hi) / 2; if mid passes then hi = mid, else lo = mid. Use the colour at hi."
    ]
  },
